# ═══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
# ELSHADAI CAKE CREATIONS — ENVIRONMENT VARIABLES
# ═══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
# Copy this file to `.env.local` and fill in the values.
# `.env.local` is git-ignored and must never be committed.
#
# Until these are set, the website runs perfectly well — the reviews section
# simply says it is not connected yet. Nothing else is affected.
#
# Note: there is deliberately NO service-role key here. Review submission is
# protected by row level security and owner actions run under the owner's own
# login, so this website never needs a key that can bypass database security.
# ═══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════

# Your Supabase project URL.
# Supabase dashboard -> Project Settings -> Data API
NEXT_PUBLIC_SUPABASE_URL=

# The PUBLIC anonymous key. Safe to expose in the browser — it is restricted by
# row level security and cannot read customer email addresses.
# Supabase dashboard -> Project Settings -> API Keys -> anon / public
NEXT_PUBLIC_SUPABASE_ANON_KEY=

# A long random string used to hash submitter addresses for rate limiting.
# Generate one with:
#   node -e "console.log(require('crypto').randomBytes(32).toString('hex'))"
# Keep it secret, and do not change it after launch or existing throttling
# records stop matching.
REVIEW_HASH_SALT=
